    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Data Collection Facts Label\"\nformat:\n  html\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n\n<style>\ntable.nutrition-label {\n  width: 75%;\n  border-collapse: collapse;\n  border: 2px solid black;\n  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  font-size: 12px;\n  margin-left: auto;\n  margin-right: auto;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label th,\ntable.nutrition-label td {\n  border: 1px solid black;\n  padding: 5px 7px;\n}\n\ntable.nutrition-label thead tr:nth-child(2) {\n  display: none;\n}\n</style>\n<table class=\"nutrition-label\">\n <thead>\n<tr><th style=\"border-bottom:hidden;padding-bottom:0; padding-left:3px;padding-right:3px;text-align: center; font-weight: bold; color: white !important;padding-right: 4px; padding-left: 4px; background-color: black !important;font-size: 18px;\" colspan=\"2\"><div style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 5px; \">Data Source Facts Label</div></th></tr>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\">  </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 1. Source Identity </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source name </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> The American Affordability Tracker </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Domain/topic </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Cost of living </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Source type </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Institutional data / Research dataset </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 2. Collection Context </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collector/producer </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Urban Institute </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Original purpose </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> A data tool funded by Urban Institute, which is a nonprofit research organization with the goal of equipping changemakers with evidence and solutions to improve lives and strengthen communities. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Collection method </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Uses the Missouri Census Data Center’s 2022 Geographic Correspondence Engine crosswalks to convert data from Public Use Microdata Areas (PUMAs), zip codes, and counties (depending on data source) to population-weighted averages by congressional districts. Also uses population-based weights to aggregate up to the state and national levels where\nneeded. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Record-creation event </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Updated as new indicators and more recent data becomes available. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 3. Observation and Scope </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Unit of observation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> One geographic area (a national average, state or congressional district) for a specific time period </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Population or objects represented </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> U.S. households, U.S. consumers, and geographic regions </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Time period covered </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> 2017 - 2025 (varies by metric) </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Geographic area coverage </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> United States </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 4. Variables and Data Structure </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Main variables/fields </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Rent, home sale prices, gas prices, grocery prices, and average weekly earnings </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Data types included </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Numerical (dollar amounts, percentages, credit scores, etc.), text (dictionary definitions), time (months, quarters, years), and location (zip codes, counties, states, congressional districts) </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Direct measurements </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Average price per gallon of regular gas, average weekly earnings of all employees, average Vantage credit score </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Possible proxy variables </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Thrifty Food Plan market basket for a family of four is used as a stand in for general grocery costs. </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;height: 26px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \"> 5. Documentation </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;color: white !important;background-color: black !important;font-size: 12px;width: 50%; \">  </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Documentation found </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Technical Appendix PDF, Data dictionary CSV, ID variables dictionary CSV </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> Stated collection details </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;font-size: 11px;width: 50%; \"> All metrics are available at the national and state level. Data is provided by congressional district using fixed 119th Congress boundaries for all years. Data for some congressional districts may not be available. </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n",
